    "ai_need_web_classifier": "You are a lightweight classifier (not answering the question).\n\nUser research question:\n\"{{query}}\"\n\nDecide whether a good answer requires **current or external factual information from the web** (news, laws, statistics, product specs, sports results, precise dates/events, paper citations, etc.).\n\nSet need_web = **true** when missing or stale facts would materially hurt the answer.\nSet need_web = **false** when careful reasoning, conceptual analysis, ethics, creativity, or introspection suffices—e.g. purely philosophical questions like the meaning of life, open-ended \"how should I think about…\", or fiction—without needing verified external facts.\n\nWhen unsure, prefer **true**.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON, no markdown fences or explanation:\n{\"need_web\": true}\nor\n{\"need_web\": false}",
    "ai_decompose_question": "You are a rigorous researcher. The overarching question the user wants to understand is: \"{{query}}\"\n\nBreak this large question into 3–5 logically progressive sub-questions. Requirements:\n- Each sub-question must be something research must answer—not a writing step or an instruction to find sources.\n- Sub-questions should advance logically (e.g., phenomenon → causes, facts → interpretation, parts → wholes, or another progression suited to the topic).\n- Phrase each sub-question the way a real person would ask—not in academic paper title style.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON array, no extra text:\n\n[\n  {\"title\": \"Full wording of sub-question 1\", \"desc\": \"Why this step is logically necessary and what it clarifies\"},\n  {\"title\": \"Full wording of sub-question 2\", \"desc\": \"Why this step is logically necessary and what it clarifies\"},\n  {\"title\": \"Full wording of sub-question 3\", \"desc\": \"Why this step is logically necessary and what it clarifies\"}\n]",
    "ai_revise_decompose": "You are a rigorous researcher. You previously broke down \"{{query}}\" into the following sub-questions:\n\n{{plan}}\n\nThe user's feedback on this breakdown:\n{{instruction}}\n\nAdjust the sub-question breakdown according to the feedback. Keep these constraints:\n- Each sub-question must require research to answer—not a writing step or an instruction to find sources.\n- Sub-questions must advance logically.\n- Natural phrasing—avoid thesis-title tone.\n- Keep 3–5 sub-questions unless the user explicitly asks otherwise.\n\nReturn ONLY valid JSON array:\n[\n  {\"title\": \"…\", \"desc\": \"…\"}\n]",
